      "side": 1,
      "message": "The right boundary check is missing the block width (`bw`). `aom_int_pro_row` projects a 2D block into a 1D array by reading up to `search_size_width_right + bw` pixels to the right of the block\u0027s left edge (`mi_col \u003c\u003c 2`). If `(mi_col \u003c\u003c 2) + search_size_width_right` reaches `cm-\u003ewidth + border`, the search will read `bw` pixels past the padded border, leading to out-of-bounds reads into uninitialized memory or the next row\u0027s padding.\n\nTo fix this, you should move the declarations of `bw` and `bh` (currently at lines 2213-2214) to before these checks, and include them:\n```c\n    if (((mi_col \u003c\u003c 2) + search_size_width_right + bw) \u003e cm-\u003ewidth + border) {\n      search_size_width_right \u003d\n          AOMMAX(0, cm-\u003ewidth + border - (mi_col \u003c\u003c 2) - bw);\n    }\n```\nThe `AOMMAX` is needed to prevent `search_size_width_right` from becoming negative if the block overhangs the border.\n\nYou should also fix the `else` block to include `bw` in its condition.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2153,
        "startChar": -1,
        "endLine": 2153,
        "endChar": 0
      },
